      ":question/worked-solution": "Collect the common factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&-\\frac{3}{2}\\sin^2\\left(140^\\circ\\right)+\\frac{3}{2}\\cos^2\\left(140^\\circ\\right)\\\\&=\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\cos^2\\left(140^\\circ\\right)-\\sin^2\\left(140^\\circ\\right)\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the cosine double-angle formula:\n\n$$\n\\cos^2 x-\\sin^2 x=\\cos(2x)\n$$\n\nSubstitute $x=140^\\circ$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos^2\\left(140^\\circ\\right)-\\sin^2\\left(140^\\circ\\right)&=\\cos\\left(2\\cdot 140^\\circ\\right)\\\\&=\\cos\\left(280^\\circ\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKeep the outside factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\cos^2\\left(140^\\circ\\right)-\\sin^2\\left(140^\\circ\\right)\\right)&=\\frac{3}{2}\\cos\\left(280^\\circ\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
